p":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3300056041","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110554#issuecomment-3300056041","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110554","id":3300056041,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Estvp","user":{"login":"TheGrandJonsson","id":31918672,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxOTE4Njcy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/31918672?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheGrandJonsson","html_url":"https://github.com/TheGrandJonsson","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheGrandJonsson/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheGrandJonsson/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheGrandJonsson/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheGrandJonsson/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheGrandJonsson/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheGrandJonsson/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheGrandJonsson/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheGrandJonsson/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheGrandJonsson/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-16T19:24:45Z","updated_at":"2025-09-16T19:24:45Z","body":"\n> Just chiming in with some potentially helpful info.\n> \n> I've had this issue during 4.5 beta phases and found out the character was a \"Six-Per-Em Space (U+2006)\" (decimal 8198).\n> \n> That was missing in my font file, and I was seeing an unknown char. I fixed it by adding a range of “invisible” characters to the font file, namely decimal range 8192-8203.\n> \n> Using a fully-featured `.ttf` file (e.g., just a simple `Arial.ttf` from your system) does not show this additional character in your MRP — can you double-check?\n\nYou might be right, checked with a different font and with my new font it works as intended. Which means there might be a character in the ttf that Godot 4.5 interprets different. Opened the font in question in fontlab 8 tried editing and deleting stuff until something worked. \nSeems like it's the space character that's the culprit. U0020. \nRemoving the SPACE character from the .ttf file seems to fix the issue, however now I don't have a space =) \nI tried adding a NOBREAKSPACE 00A0, but that didn't solve it. \nFor some reason it seems like Godot 4.4 was more lenient when it came to font files. I tried re-encoding the font file as well in unicode latin-standard. But that didn't do anything either. \n\nI can try more things tomorrow, however I'm not that good with how fonts works so I might be completely off base here. \n\n\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3300056041/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3300720467","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110554#issuecomment-3300720467","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110554","id":3300720467,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7EvP9T","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_u